<item><title>Libya&apos;s interior minister reviews Jufra security and desert rally plans</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-s-interior-minister-reviews-jufra-security-and-desert-1a6c45/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-s-interior-minister-reviews-jufra-security-and-desert-1a6c45/</guid><category>Libya</category><description>Essam Abu Zriba met parliament member Muadh Rafaa to discuss security in Jufra and the southern region, including a plan to secure a desert rally.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:39:34 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ly.jpg" length="30956" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ly.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Eastern Libyan government orders joint inquiry into attack on Russian vessel</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/eastern-libyan-government-orders-joint-inquiry-into-attack-aedb16/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/eastern-libyan-government-orders-joint-inquiry-into-attack-aedb16/</guid><category>Libya</category><description>Officials suspect unmanned vehicles struck the ship at Benghazi port, where it had stopped to refuel and take on supplies before returning to Russia.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:01:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ly.jpg" length="30956" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ly.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Libya sets catch-up timetables for schools that opened late</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-sets-catch-up-timetables-for-schools-that-opened-late-08e233/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-sets-catch-up-timetables-for-schools-that-opened-late-08e233/</guid><category>Libya</category><description>Under the new plan, the education ministry says late-opening schools must still cover the prescribed syllabus before the 2026–27 year closes.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ly.jpg" length="30956" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ly.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Libya ranks second in Africa with 146.7 tonnes of central bank gold</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-ranks-second-in-africa-with-146-7-tonnes-of-central-9dc51d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-ranks-second-in-africa-with-146-7-tonnes-of-central-9dc51d/</guid><category>Libya</category><description>Algeria leads the continent with 173.6 tonnes, while Libya has virtually no industrial gold mining, according to figures cited in a report.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:08:16 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-ranks-second-in-africa-with-146-7-tonnes-of-central-9dc51d/share.jpg" length="42802" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ly/libya-ranks-second-in-africa-with-146-7-tonnes-of-central-9dc51d/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
